Subject: The profiler counts how often a global read's cache cell was filled

What this does
  - `regvm_global_site_fill` records the generation of the global-cell cache it filled the site at
    as a distinct "shape" of that site (profile builds only), so a site filled at two generations
    shows two entries.

Why we need it
  A compiled global read whose cache cell misses leaves the body (so it is no safepoint for the
  facts about objects). That is cheap only if misses are rare; a site that was refilled after the
  global object changed during the profiled run keeps the continuing form.

--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -16117,6 +16117,9 @@
     e->gslot = slot;
     e->slot_off = gen;
     e->kind = REG_PIC_GLOBAL;
+    /* The profile counts the distinct generations a site was filled at: a site filled
+       twice saw the global object change. */
+    AOT_PROF_PIC(b, site, (JSShape *)(uintptr_t)((uintptr_t)gen + 1), REG_PIC_GLOBAL);
 }
 #endif
 
